    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="2" relname="circumstance">In any time when you one is developing applications, software, or any other  UI,</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="16" relname="span">there are a series of tests before it is introduced to the user.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="4" relname="concession">Despite the programmer's error,</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="13" relname="span">a good QA team would have picked up this error.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="15" relname="span">However, I believe the development box was not properly configured for the programmer to do his job.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="7" relname="circumstance">When one is developing any application,</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="14" relname="span">one has the ability to read, write, and delete any data is a system withouth destroying the true data.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="17" relname="span">You are probably right about him being rushed</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="8" relname="nonvolitional-cause">because he would have picked this up.</segment>
        <group id="10" type="span"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="10" relname="span"/>
        <group id="12" type="span" parent="11" relname="span"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="12" relname="span"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="5" relname="nonvolitional-cause"/>
